.TH "tangsible-view" "1" "2026-11-26" "Tangsible" "Tangsible Manual"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
tangsible-view - browse a playbook'\&s plays and tasks without running anything
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBtangsible view\fR [--ee \fIimage\fR | --no-ee] [\fIansible-playbook options\fR .\&.\&.\&] [\fIplaybook.\&yml\fR]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBview\fR shows what a playbook would do, as the tree \fBtangsible-run\fR(1) and
\fBtangsible-debug\fR(1) show while it runs - plays and their tasks, without any
host lines - but runs nothing.\& If \fIplaybook.\&yml\fR is omitted, it is resolved
the same way as \fBtangsible-run\fR(1) (see \fBtangsible\fR(1)).\&
.PP
The playbook is read the way \fBansible-playbook\fR(1) reads it: roles, blocks,
imports and the order of \fBpre_tasks\fR, roles, \fBtasks\fR and \fBpost_tasks\fR are as
Ansible resolves them.\& Only what is known without running can be shown: a
task pulled in by \fBinclude_tasks\fR is not expanded (the include itself is a
row), and a templated host pattern or task name is shown as written.\&
Handlers are not listed.\&
.PP
\fBEnter\fR (or a click) on a task opens a view with three tabs:
.PP
\fBTask\fR
.RS 4
The task'\&s name, its role (if any), its action, the \fBHosts:\fR of its play
as written (for example \fIweb:!\&db1\fR), and its \fBwhen:\fR conditions and tags
if it has any.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBTask definition\fR
.RS 4
The task'\&s source from its file; click a key in it for what it means.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBDocs\fR
.RS 4
\fBansible-doc\fR(1) for the task'\&s action.\&
.PP
.RE
Standard \fBansible-playbook\fR(1) arguments can be given; they are kept for
\fBr\fR.\& \fB--ee\fR and \fB--no-ee\fR are understood as for \fBtangsible-run\fR(1): the
playbook is then read inside the execution environment.\&
.PP
.SH KEY BINDINGS
.PP
\fBUp/Down, Page Up/Down, CTRL-B/F, Home/End, CTRL-A/E\fR
.RS 4
Move the selection in the tree.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBEnter\fR
.RS 4
Open the selected task.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBRight/Left\fR
.RS 4
Nothing to expand in the tree: there are no host lines.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB/\fR
.RS 4
Search the tree.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBr\fR
.RS 4
Open the re-run dialog; confirming it runs the playbook (\fBtangsible-run\fR(1))
in this same session, with the tags and limit entered there.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBe\fR
.RS 4
In the task view, open the task'\&s source file in \fB$VISUAL\fR / \fB$EDITOR\fR.\&
When the editor returns the playbook is read again (see \fBR\fR).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBR\fR
.RS 4
Read the playbook again, in the tree and in the task view, and show the
new version: the cursor and the open task stay on the same task (found by
play, name and position among tasks of that name), and say so if it is
gone.\& A playbook that no longer loads leaves the old version in place and
shows the reason in the bottom bar.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBTab / Shift-Tab\fR
.RS 4
In the task view, switch tabs.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBRight/Left, n / N\fR
.RS 4
In the task view, the next / previous task (\fBn\fR / \fBN\fR step through matches
instead while a search has matches).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBEsc\fR
.RS 4
Back from the task view.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBq / Ctrl-C\fR
.RS 4
Quit.\&
.PP
.RE
The keys \fBf\fR (filter), \fBo\fR (raw output) and \fBs\fR (statistics) belong to a run
and do nothing here.\&
.PP
.SH EXIT STATUS
.PP
\fB0\fR
.RS 4
Normal exit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB1\fR
.RS 4
The playbook couldn'\&t be read.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB2\fR
.RS 4
Usage error.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBtangsible\fR(1), \fBtangsible-run\fR(1), \fBtangsible-debug\fR(1)
